{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass on the third day, when they were in pain.</b> It is known from the way of the wisdom of nature that the third day is weak in all created beings, whether it is the third day after birth or the third day of the days of the world, for the third day is the star Mars, and because of this the pain intensifies in every wound on the third day, and one who is circumcised will be weaker on the third day after circumcision. And our Sages said that it is permissible to do for a circumcision that falls on Shabbat on the third day after circumcision everything he needs, just as on a weekday, because he is in danger on the third day more than on all other days. And the masters of astronomy wrote that the third day's sign is Scorpio, and its king is Samael, and its minister is Mars. And from this our Sages, of blessed memory, said (Ta'anit 27b): the men of the ma'amad did not fast on Sunday because it is the third day to the formation — meaning, to the formation of the first man, who was created on the sixth day. And this is the reason for the blessing over fragrant woods at the departure of Shabbat, in order to strengthen the power of the rational soul with a good fragrance." "<b>And the two sons of Jacob, Shimon and Levi, took.</b> From the verses we can learn how many years they had when they destroyed Shechem. It is known that Jacob was in the house of Laban twenty years, fourteen for his two daughters and six years for his flocks, and after seven years that he served for Rachel, Laban deceived him and gave him Leah, and she gave birth to Reuben in seven months, and after him Shimon was born at seven months. It is found that when Jacob parted from Laban at the end of twenty years, Shimon was twelve years old less two months. Jacob tarried at Sukkot eighteen months and came to Shechem; it is found that Shimon was thirteen years and four months old, and Levi twelve years and nine months old. And Scripture calls them 'men,' as it is written: ״ויקחו שמעון ולוי איש חרבו״ — 'Shimon and Levi took, each man his sword,' etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:17:39.272160139Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}